Explain time-travel debugging in Redux.

Time-travel debugging in Redux lets you go back and forth through the history of actions in the Redux store. It helps you understand how the application’s state changes over time and makes it easier to pinpoint and fix bugs by replaying specific scenarios. It’s like rewinding and fast-forwarding through time to see how the state evolves.

