What are Redux middleware composition.

Redux middleware composition is refers to the process of combining multiple middleware functions to enhance the behavior of the Redux store. Each middleware function can modify actions, perform tasks like logging or asynchronous operations, and pass the action along to the next middleware. By chaining these functions together, developers can create custom pipelines to handle various aspects of action processing, making it easier to manage complex logic and extend the capabilities of Redux.

